# Sanity

- Sanity is the CMS and source of truth for website content.
- Use the existing Sanity project. Never create a new Sanity project automatically.
- Never expose Sanity private/write credentials to the browser. Keep Sanity server credentials on the server only.
- Inspect existing Sanity schemas before creating new schemas. Avoid duplicate content models.
- Document every Sanity schema or data-model change.
- User accounts must not be stored as plaintext credentials in Sanity.
